---

A short field guide to the mistakes that are easy to make and easy to fix.

## Do not mutate captured host state

```svelte
<!-- ✗ writes to a serialized snapshot -->
<button onclick={() => count++}>{count}</button>
```

If `count` is captured from the host, this is a snapshot. Own the state inside the island instead, or pass it as a prop and mutate island-local state.

## Functions and snippets do not cross

You cannot hand an island a callback or a snippet from the host. Model the interaction with props and remote functions, or move the UI inside the island.

## Page lifecycle will not run

`onMount` in a `csr = false` page is dead code. If you reach for it, you actually want an island.

## Reach for an island, not a dynamic import

If you find yourself hand-rolling `import()` + mount to lazy-load a component, that is what `wake: 'idle'` / `'visible'` already do — with SSR HTML first and a signed boundary.

## Pick the boundary before you build

Decide up front: interactive → island; static-but-heavy inside an island → [lake](/docs/islands/lakes); request-dependent HTML → [server island](/docs/islands/server-islands). Retrofitting the boundary later is the expensive path.

## Remember dev is not prod

Query seeding and the mutation guard behave differently in dev. If something works in `dev` but you are unsure, check a production build before shipping.
